51
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:57,993
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Comoughs.

52
00:04:59,933 --> 00:05:05,317
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Sa ating mga magigiting na miyembro ng Kagawaran ng Tanggulang Pambansa.

53
00:05:05,317 --> 00:05:07,223
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Tangsandatahang lakas ng Pilipinas.

54
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:15,020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: sa pumumuno ng ating kalihim, Secretary Gilberto C. Chidoro,

55
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:19,694
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: AFP Chief of Staff General Antonio Nafarete,

56
00:05:20,842 --> 00:05:25,735
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: at mga pinuno ng ating mga kawanihan at attached agencies,

57
00:05:26,917 --> 00:05:32,671
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: maligayang pagdating po dito sa Kongreso at isang magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

58
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:38,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It is my privilege to welcome the Department of National Defense

59
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:45,698
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to the Committee on Appropriations as we begin deliberations on its proposed Fiscal Year 2027 budget.

60
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:56,313
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For Fiscal Year 2027, the Department of National Defense is proposing a budget of $324.63 billion,

61
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:02,455
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: reflecting the government's continuing commitment to our national security,

62
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,623
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: territorial integrity, and the protection of our people.

63
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:13,897
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This is complemented by $132.59 billion,

64
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:21,727
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: of which $50 billion is allocated for the revised AFP modernization program

65
00:06:22,319 --> 00:06:28,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to support the acquisition and the upgrading of equipment and systems necessary

66
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:34,568
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to keep our armed forces capable and responsive to the security challenges of our time.

67
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:42,880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The remaining $82.59 billion is allocated to the equally important pensions

68
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,655
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: of our veterans and AFP retirees.

69
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:53,452
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: These are significant investments, but national defense is not measured by numbers alone.

70
00:06:54,880 --> 00:07:00,742
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It is ultimately about the men and women who stand ready to serve our country.

71
00:07:01,599 --> 00:07:05,551
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Our maritime domain remains contested.

72
00:07:06,639 --> 00:07:13,955
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And the men and women who hold our position there have done so with a steadiness

73
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,465
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: this country has to pause to acknowledge.

74
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,802
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Through the leadership of Secretary Chodoro,

75
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:26,138
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: our partnerships with like-minded nations have deepened,

76
00:07:27,199 --> 00:07:33,614
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and our forces have carried the weight professionally and well.

77
00:07:35,759 --> 00:07:39,571
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Our soldiers continue to bear internal security,

78
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:47,131
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and in every community struck by earthquake, by flood, by storm,

79
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:51,620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it is the men in uniform that arrive first.

80
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:58,403
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: I say that not as a matter of record, but because I've seen that firsthand.

81
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:03,520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: In the middle of the series of earthquakes and monsoon rains

82
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:07,077
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: that struck our communities in the 2nd District of Sultan Kudarat,

83
00:08:09,199 --> 00:08:11,195
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: that is what this budget is for.

84
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:20,155
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Not platforms, not line items, but the fact that when this country is at its most frightened,

85
00:08:21,039 --> 00:08:26,129
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it sends the men and women of the Department of National Defense forward.

86
00:08:27,039 --> 00:08:27,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And they go.

87
00:08:29,039 --> 00:08:34,702
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And when they do, we must give and arm them with the capabilities to do so.

88
00:08:36,399 --> 00:08:40,034
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It means seeing the modernization of the armed forces through.

89
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:47,760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Republic Act No. 10349, or the Revised AFP Modernization Act of 2012,

90
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:52,336
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: approaches the end of its term, and the work it began is not finished.

91
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:01,600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Congress and this representation will support a modernization program carried to completion

92
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:08,131
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: rather than left at its most expensive and at least useful stage, which is halfway.

93
00:09:10,959 --> 00:09:16,480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That law and how the ongoing modernization program is financed

94
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:20,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: are among the most consequential questions of national security

95
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:24,314
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: that should be at the forefront of national policy discussions.

96
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:33,275
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: At an age where threats to our sovereignty have morphed from conventional military threats

97
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:38,236
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to hybrid tactics, cyber intrusion, disinformation,

98
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,590
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: gray zone activities,

99
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:47,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: we need to support investments in our technical capacities

100
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:52,934
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and in those that safeguard our defense establishment in all its forms.

101
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:59,836
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Let us therefore ensure that this fiscal year 2027 national budget

102
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:04,257
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: supports a stronger, more modern armed forces,

103
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:08,560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: a more empowered Office of Civil Defense,

104
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:15,698
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you.

105
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:24,895
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: May we now invite Secretary Teodoro to proceed with the presentation of the budget of the Department of National Defense.

106
00:10:25,410 --> 00:10:28,970
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you to our distinguished sponsors, Madam Vice Chair,

107
00:10:29,290 --> 00:10:31,870
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the Honorable Representative Suansing,

108
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:35,050
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the, uh, Deputy Speakers present,

109
00:10:35,950 --> 00:10:37,470
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: members of the majority,

110
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:39,430
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and distinguished members of the minority,

111
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:40,590
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and former colleagues.

112
00:10:40,590 --> 00:10:43,200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: A pleasant good morning to each and every one of you.

113
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's once again an honor to be here.

114
00:10:46,490 --> 00:10:52,090
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And, um, may I, uh, first thank the Honorable Vice Chair

115
00:10:52,090 --> 00:11:04,570
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: for messaging that she realizes that modernization happens really very quickly nowadays,

116
00:11:05,710 --> 00:11:08,390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: particularly with the advance in technology.

117
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:11,410
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the latest,

118
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:20,490
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the latest calculations we have is that for commanders in the forefront of highly technical war,

119
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:27,530
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the response actions to include the legal framework,

120
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:33,930
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the response time is as quick as three seconds to respond.

121
00:11:33,930 --> 00:11:38,690
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That is the kind of environment that we are facing.

122
00:11:39,830 --> 00:11:40,730
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And yet,

123
00:11:41,230 --> 00:11:42,630
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the modernization law,

124
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:46,490
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: has us working on 15-year horizons where,

125
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:47,090
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: you know,

126
00:11:47,090 --> 00:11:53,750
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: fads really fade faster than 15 years.

127
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:54,590
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So I'm very,

128
00:11:54,590 --> 00:12:04,550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: very happy that the Honorable Vice Chair has messaged or signaled the willingness of Congress to adapt to a more adaptive,

129
00:12:04,550 --> 00:12:05,210
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: flexible,

130
00:12:05,210 --> 00:12:08,750
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and agile system and a more operationally secure one.

131
00:12:10,470 --> 00:12:12,350
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So,

132
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:20,290
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: let us probably go to the meat of our presentation since the prefatory portion.

133
00:12:20,430 --> 00:12:21,050
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

134
00:12:21,050 --> 00:12:27,190
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We, we, uh, uh, of course,

135
00:12:27,310 --> 00:12:34,490
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the mandate is already known under Executive Order 292 and other laws of the department.

136
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:39,070
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I propose,

137
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:41,690
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: if your honor please,

138
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:45,150
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: that we go to the major thrusts,

139
00:12:45,450 --> 00:12:53,310
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in order for us to address the individual concerns of the members with more time.

140
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:55,510
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, for the major thrusts,

141
00:12:55,510 --> 00:12:59,010
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

142
00:12:59,010 --> 00:13:05,360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For sovereignty and territorial integrity,

143
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:08,000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which is, uh, a [unclear] mission area,

144
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which is a new mission area for us,

145
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: given the fact that now we realize that we have

146
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:28,020
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: 2.4 million square kilometers of maritime domain that we must, uh... uh, make, uh, have overwatch over.

147
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:46,820
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And secondly to try to preempt any efforts to remove from the jurisdiction of the Philippines the exploration and exploitation of the same.

148
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:47,820
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

149
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:56,020
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Although the major focus right now, naturally, is the West Philippine Sea as an area of contest.

150
00:13:56,020 --> 00:14:06,330
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: A bigger domain actually is the Pacific Ocean and the Philippine Rise of which we must start already building our infrastructure,

151
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:19,330
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: start our logistical bases in central areas with access that are accessible to the equipment that are germane to the armed forces of the Philippines,

152
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:27,390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and proceed to constructing our strategic bases which will allow us to have presence in that maritime domain.

153
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:34,090
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To even make sure that we have ready and reliable supply chains,

154
00:14:34,090 --> 00:14:39,770
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which is an essential exercise this day and age.

155
00:14:39,770 --> 00:14:41,390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

156
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:51,490
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: An area which we cannot vacate for quite some time,

157
00:14:51,490 --> 00:14:59,970
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: particularly as we know that it is essential for us to have robust and

158
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:12,280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and substantial presence in majority of the islands of the Philippines in order to deter any recurrence of violence,

159
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:22,640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to prevent the resurgence of violence, and to be able to assist communities immediately when they are in need.

160
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:36,000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And since the threat of malign activities occurring in uninhabited areas is real, therefore some presence in those areas is necessary.

161
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:43,720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, the internal security and stability role remains germane to the external defense role

162
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:52,520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because without internal peace and stability, we cannot build a core for external defense.

163
00:15:52,640 --> 00:16:06,280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So this remains a priority area, and we are very proactive right now in the BARMM area

164
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:21,240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because of the fact that we realize it's going to be the first democratic exercise of any of the 22 peace processes that the UN recognizes.

165
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:35,180
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And, uh, we devote, uh, a big amount of, uh, resources in personnel and in MOOE under the supervision and control of the Commission on Elections

166
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:43,680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in order to help deter unwanted election-related or non-related violence in the area.

167
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:45,900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next.

168
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:53,900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Welfare of veterans is extremely important because the veterans, although they are retired,

169
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:59,380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They remain a moral force and a driving force even if they are retired.

170
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:05,520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They serve as valuable additions to the active duty forces,

171
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:17,160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: particularly those with technical skills and expertise who we still rely on in order to provide leadership to junior personnel.

172
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:24,160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, also the President has approved the first stage of the...

173
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:30,940
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: construction of an annex in the Veterans Memorial Medical Center

174
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:34,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which will allow us to move our current patients

175
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:41,340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: so that the rehabilitation of the legacy building which is more than 70 years old

176
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:50,120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and the structure being unsustainable and the cost of a high infection rate can be commenced

177
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:54,080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and can be, uh, optimized for use.

178
00:17:54,080 --> 00:18:02,960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thirdly, the President has continued appropriations for what we call Valor Clinics,

179
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:13,740
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: external clinics where we can service veterans closer to where they are situated.

180
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:22,960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: However, the challenge we face is to staff these...

181
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:32,700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: these clinics with competent personnel who are also security vetted in order to handle medical and data privacy issues.

182
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:39,000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, we, by the end of the year, will have three to five running.

183
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:47,120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Fortunately, we are able to get some personnel and as we are able to fill these up sustainably,

184
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: this will be a program that will continue.

185
00:18:52,960 --> 00:19:00,120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, the health care of veterans is now being merged

186
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:06,780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in the wellness and preventive health care side with those in the active duty

187
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:14,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: so that in the active duty, we can mitigate with preventive health care

188
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:22,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: those diseases that may be mitigated during the time...

189
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:31,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That they are still young and they do not manifest as severely when they reach retirement age.

190
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:47,340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we have special programs too for the veterans and senior citizens on other issues that we may not have addressed before.

191
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:55,300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For example, mental wellness, mental health, and geriatric care issues.

192
00:19:58,020 --> 00:20:06,120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That basically forms the core of the Veterans Welfare Program for us.

193
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:16,140
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We also realize that for veterans, it's quite important for them to be able to socialize and to have an ecosystem after they retire.

194
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:22,360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: As we know, retirement from the military service is a traumatic issue.

195
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:33,840
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Actually, it's a traumatic incident because for 40 years, 30 years of your life, you are in a structured environment with a support system.

196
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,180
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Then suddenly, the next day, this is cut off.

197
00:20:36,817 --> 00:21:17,857
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, we need to provide for that transition and the post-retirement [unclear] wellness of the veteran. We're able to approach it in a more holistic manner now. We are trying to come to grips with the issue of mental wellness in active-duty service, where we see cases right now. The incidence of violence is very low.

198
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:42,450
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But we see the incidence of inability to cope with stressful issues on a personal level, which we need to address. And we're seeing more and more of that. I think it's a phenomenon that is common to all organizations.

199
00:21:42,450 --> 00:22:04,850
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So that's basically the thrust in veterans' welfare. Next slide. On modernizing the armed forces, it is indeed a tough nut to crack, admittedly. And as the day goes on, things get more expensive.

200
00:22:04,850 --> 00:22:14,850
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We are first focusing on our core systems. Those are the foundational systems we need in order to...

201
00:22:15,170 --> 00:22:36,790
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ...building block a sustainable defense system. The equipment we use is just the tip of the spear. But without the support systems for those pieces of hardware you see, everything will be just useless because they will be unsustainable.

202
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:44,470
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And in modernizing the armed forces, there's another factor that needs to be taken into consideration.

203
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:55,870
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is the infrastructure we have to house, to support, and to maintain these capabilities, which is sadly lacking in our budget.

204
00:22:56,150 --> 00:23:06,430
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because for several years, the capital outlay has not been financed, and it's totally on modernizing.

205
00:23:06,970 --> 00:23:09,550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So it's equipment-heavy but not support-heavy.

206
00:23:09,550 --> 00:23:14,550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That goes with our authorized troop strength also, where the operating...

207
00:23:15,170 --> 00:23:21,310
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ...to support ratio is about 70-30 or 80-20, and we badly need support personnel.

208
00:23:22,810 --> 00:23:26,210
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we really badly need more troops to rotate our troops.

209
00:23:26,350 --> 00:23:29,930
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They don't have a break anymore with the mission areas that they go to.

210
00:23:31,070 --> 00:23:42,390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So modernization is a question of really building core systems, which we are prioritizing now, our IT and cyber systems for command and control.

211
00:23:42,560 --> 00:24:04,531
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: These cost less but are more critical to us because as foundational systems, any compromise in the early stage, you cannot patch anymore on a later stage because the compromise is already present.

212
00:24:05,430 --> 00:24:18,660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We are also heavily also trying to increase our capacity.

213
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:31,280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For humanitarian assistance and disaster response, you know, we have about 46 Black Hawk helicopters, which help us a lot, but that's not enough.

214
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:41,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We need larger rotary platforms in order to service with bigger weight and with pallets.

215
00:24:41,220 --> 00:24:47,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because the Black Hawk, although it can carry a lot, it needs to be loaded by hand.

216
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It cannot be palletized.

217
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:53,990
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we need palletized aircraft already on [unclear].

218
00:24:54,000 --> 00:25:01,980
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: On the naval side, we continue to acquire modern corvettes and frigates.

219
00:25:01,980 --> 00:25:21,410
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And on the army side, the first priority really is to make them more mobile so that their ability to respond and to deter in areas,

220
00:25:21,670 --> 00:25:44,970
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think we agreed with the army that the first thing that they have to do for both internal security and for external defense is to increase their footprint throughout the Philippines.

221
00:25:47,130 --> 00:25:50,670
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: This is because they serve also as logistical bases.

222
00:25:51,670 --> 00:25:55,730
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To support the frontline troops, which are badly lacking at this time.

223
00:25:57,310 --> 00:26:03,870
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: This is not the day and age of notional inventories or just in time, but it's a question of reserves and stores.

224
00:26:04,870 --> 00:26:15,670
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We need to build our strategic reserve points of storage for critical items that we need.

225
00:26:16,710 --> 00:26:20,590
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And this must be distributed throughout the Philippines.

226
00:26:21,670 --> 00:26:27,850
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: With infrastructure that can support the weight of the capabilities we carry.

227
00:26:27,850 --> 00:26:34,070
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So the modernization is not merely a question of acquiring capabilities,

228
00:26:34,830 --> 00:26:43,080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: but also providing the adequate infrastructure to support capabilities.

229
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:52,380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And secondly, providing the access to these capabilities,

230
00:26:53,080 --> 00:27:02,250
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: that can support the dimensions and the weight of the equipment that you intend to use.

